---

The only substantive changes are these. `CleanedEmail` is gone from `OUT` entirely, and the output array and `setValues` call are back to 6 columns. The email copy now writes directly to the raw `COL.email` column (C) on superseded rows via a single-cell `setValue` — only when the winner has a usable email and the target cell is empty, same guard as before. The header check is unchanged in logic (it was already `every`), but the range is correctly back to 6 columns so it won't accidentally read into W.

One thing to be aware of: writing the winner's email back into column C means it modifies raw data. If you'd rather keep C untouched, the alternative is to include email in the cleaned block but not expose it as a visible output column — just let it live in a hidden column. Let me know if you'd prefer that approach.
